{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:asymptotic-ray-exists","title":"lem:asymptotic-ray-exists","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.md","line":321,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex#lem:asymptotic-ray-exists","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:asymptotic-ray]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:has-min-segments]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:metric-limit-of-minimizing]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","label":"lem:asymptotic-ray-exists","line":549,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[Existence of asymptotic rays]\n\\label{lem:asymptotic-ray-exists}\n\n\\source{morgan-tian}\n\\uses{def:asymptotic-ray, def:has-min-segments}\n\n\n\n\n\nIn a proper metric space with minimizing segments, every $x$ is the\ninitial point of a ray asymptotic to any prescribed minimizing ray\n$\\lambda$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n\n\\uses{lem:metric-limit-of-minimizing}\nTake minimizing segments from $x$ to $\\lambda(n)$. Their lengths tend\nto infinity, and Lemma~\\ref{lem:metric-limit-of-minimizing} supplies a\nlocally uniform subsequential limit.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[Existence of asymptotic rays] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6173796d70746f7469632d7261792d657869737473\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">morgan-tian</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Aasymptotic-ray\">↗ def:asymptotic-ray</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Ahas-min-segments\">↗ def:has-min-segments</a> <p></p>In a proper metric space with minimizing segments, every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x$\">$x$</span> is the initial point of a ray asymptotic to any prescribed minimizing ray <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\lambda $\">$\\lambda $</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch </p><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Ametric-limit-of-minimizing\">↗ lem:metric-limit-of-minimizing</a> Take minimizing segments from <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x$\">$x$</span> to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\lambda (n)$\">$\\lambda (n)$</span>. Their lengths tend to infinity, and Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Ametric-limit-of-minimizing\" data-tex-node=\"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:metric-limit-of-minimizing\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6d65747269632d6c696d69742d6f662d6d696e696d697a696e67\">1</a> supplies a locally uniform subsequential limit. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:asymptotic-ray","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:asymptotic-ray","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:asymptotic-ray","title":"def:asymptotic-ray","label":"def:asymptotic-ray"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:has-min-segments","title":"def:has-min-segments","label":"def:has-min-segments"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:metric-limit-of-minimizing","title":"lem:metric-limit-of-minimizing","label":"lem:metric-limit-of-minimizing"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-gradient-norm-one","title":"lem:busemann-gradient-norm-one","label":"lem:busemann-gradient-norm-one"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#line","title":"line","label":"line"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:asymptotic-ray-exists","title":"lem:asymptotic-ray-exists","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[Existence of asymptotic rays]\n\\label{lem:asymptotic-ray-exists}\n\n\\source{morgan-tian}\n\\uses{def:asymptotic-ray, def:has-min-segments}\n\n\n\n\n\nIn a proper metric space with minimizing segments, every $x$ is the\ninitial point of a ray asymptotic to any prescribed minimizing ray\n$\\lambda$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n\n\\uses{lem:metric-limit-of-minimizing}\nTake minimizing segments from $x$ to $\\lambda(n)$. Their lengths tend\nto infinity, and Lemma~\\ref{lem:metric-limit-of-minimizing} supplies a\nlocally uniform subsequential limit.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:asymptotic-ray","title":"def:asymptotic-ray","descrip